\title{Crossing numbers of complete bipartite graphs: a reading forest}
\taxon{Overview}
\tag{top}
\meta{dependencies}{None.}
\meta{provenance}{Reading project based on the OpenAI preprint of 23 September 2026 and its accompanying Lean sources, pinned on 9 October 2026.}

\p{A structured reading of [the paper](cn-0042) and its proof of the Zarankiewicz formula:}

##{\operatorname{cr}(K_{m,n})=\left\lfloor\frac m2\right\rfloor\left\lfloor\frac{m-1}{2}\right\rfloor\left\lfloor\frac n2\right\rfloor\left\lfloor\frac{n-1}{2}\right\rfloor.}

\p{\strong{Start here.} [The proof introduction](cn-0070) explains the route from subspaces to crossings, introducing notation before use. [The guided reading](cn-0001) includes it with the main statement and final proof assembly. [The main theorem](cn-0007) links its complete argument, and [the Lean guide](cn-0038) maps the paper's lemmas to formal declarations.}

\ol{
\li{[Algebra: subspace interpolation and the rank-sum inequality](cn-0061).}
\li{[Topology: normalize a drawing and derive the additive block relation](cn-0060).}
\li{[The detector: barycentric weights and two-triangle interpolation](cn-0062).}
\li{[Odd-size lower bound](cn-0035), [even-size deletion](cn-0037), and [the matching upper bound](cn-0036).}
\li{[An exact four-by-four example](cn-0040), [sources and checks](cn-0039), and [references](cn-0041).}
}

